 "summary": "StarkWare's language for provable computation (STARKs) and Starknet smart contracts; Cairo 1.x is a Rust-like language with traits, generics and linear ownership that compiles through the Sierra safe IR to CASM for the Cairo CPU-style VM.",
 "status": "active",
 "defined_by": [
  "reference-implementation",
  "academic-paper"
 ],
 "file_extensions": [
  ".cairo"
 ],
 "homepage": "https://www.cairo-lang.org/",
 "influenced_by": [
  "rust"
 ],
 "level_notes": {
  "1": "The Cairo whitepaper defines the Cairo VM/AIR; there is no language specification for Cairo 1 beyond the compiler and the official Cairo Book.",
  "2": "The Cairo Book (starknet.io/cairo-book) is the official tutorial and de facto reference.",
  "0": "starkware-libs/cairo (Rust) holds the Cairo 1 compiler, Sierra and corelib; cairo-lang (Python) the legacy Cairo 0; lambdaclass/cairo-vm is an alternative VM."
 },
